QA Automation Project (Selenium + Pytest + API)

This project demonstrates end-to-end (E2E) and API testing using Python.
It focuses on real-world QA practices including structured test design, environment configuration, and stable automation.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🚀 Tech Stack
Python 3.12
Selenium
Pytest
Requests (API testing)
Allure (reporting)
python-dotenv (environment config)
Faker (test data)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
📁 Project Structure
project/
├── config/
│   └── env_config.py        # Environment config (no secrets)
├── pages/                  # Page Object Model
├── drivers/                # WebDriver setup
├── fixtures/               # Pytest fixtures
├── utils/                  # Helpers & utilities
├── data/                   # Test data & builders
├── tests/
│   ├── e2e/                # UI tests (Selenium)
│   │   ├── test_store_search.py
│   │   ├── test_store_registration.py
│   │   ├── test_store_location.py
│   │   ├── test_store_security.py
│   │   └── test_login.py
│   └── api/                # API tests (requests)
│       └── test_login_api.py
├── conftest.py             # Shared fixtures
├── pytest.ini              # Pytest config & markers
├── requirements.txt
├── .env.example            # Example environment variables
└── README.md
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⚙️ Setup

1. Install dependencies

pip install -r requirements.txt

2. Configure environment

Copy .env.example:

cp .env.example .env

Fill in your values:

DEV_API_BASE_URL=https://your-api-url
DEV_WEB_BASE_URL=https://your-web-url
DEV_PARTNER_USERNAME=your_username
DEV_PARTNER_PASSWORD=your_password
DEV_MERCHANT_USERNAME=your_username
DEV_MERCHANT_PASSWORD=your_password
DEV_DUP_USERNAME=existing_username

⚠️ .env is not committed for security reasons

🧪 Running Tests
Run all tests
pytest
Run E2E tests
pytest tests/e2e
Run API tests
pytest tests/api
Run by marker
pytest -m search
pytest -m registration
pytest -m security
pytest -m api
🏷️ Test Markers
search – store search functionality
registration – store creation & validation
security – password & account lock
api – API tests
smoke, regression, slow – execution grouping
🔑 Key Features
✅ Page Object Model (POM)

Encapsulates UI interactions for maintainability and readability.

✅ Data-driven Testing

Uses pytest.mark.parametrize for validation scenarios and edge cases.

✅ Environment-based Configuration

Separates:

UI base URL
API base URL
credentials

Using .env and env_config.py.

✅ Stable Synchronization

Implements result-based waiting instead of relying only on UI loaders to reduce flaky tests.

✅ API Testing
Login API (success & failure scenarios)
Validates both:
HTTP response
business logic (code, message)
⚠️ Notes
Sensitive data (URLs, credentials) are NOT committed.
.env.example is provided for setup reference.
Some API endpoints require valid credentials.
